, TimestampNormalizer\n      - path: pkg/testutils/build.go\n        action: create\n        note: BuildBinary helper for compiling cmd/ packages in tests\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Define the DiffTest struct with fields: Name string, Args []string, Stdin []byte,\n          Env []string, WorkDir string, ExitCode int, Normalize []NormalizeFunc,\n          ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte. Define NormalizeFunc as func([]byte) []byte.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest).\n          For each DiffTest, run both binaries with identical args, stdin, env, and working\n          directory. Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code. If Normalize functions are\n          provided, apply them to stdout and stderr before comparison. If ExpectedFiles is\n          set, compare file contents after execution. Report differences using t.Errorf with\n          the test name, input, expected output, and actual output.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc that chains\n          multiple normalizers in order. Implement TimestampNormalizer as a package-level\n          NormalizeFunc that replaces timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder so\n          time-dependent output can be compared.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string. Compile the Go package\n          at the given directory within the module using \"go build -o <tempdir>/<name> <dir>\".\n          Return the path to the compiled binary. Call t.Fatal if compilation fails. Register\n          a t.Cleanup to remove the temporary binary. The function must work from within the\n          Go module -- do not create temporary Go programs outside the module boundary.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C in the environment f