st RunDiffTests with matching binaries (e.g., use /bin/echo or /usr/bin/true as\n          both go and ref binary) to verify that identical outputs produce no test failures.\n          Use a mock testing.T or verify behavior through subprocess test patterns.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Test RunDiffTests with divergent binaries to verify that stdout, stderr, or exit\n          code differences are reported as test failures with the test name and divergent\n          output included in the error message.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Test ComposeNormalizers chains multiple normalizers in order. Test\n          TimestampNormalizer replaces common timestamp formats with a fixed placeholder\n          string and leaves non-timestamp text unchanged.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Test BuildBinary compiles a valid cmd/ package (use cmd/version if it exists, or\n          skip gracefully per CLAUDE.md if no cmd/ package has source). Verify the returned\n          path points to an executable file. Verify compilation failure causes t.Fatal.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Tests for RunDiffTests use real system binaries (/bin/echo, /usr/bin/true) rather\n          than building Go binaries, to avoid circular dependencies on BuildBinary.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          If no cmd/ package has Go source files (generation run state), tests that require\n          BuildBinary skip gracefully with t.Skip per CLAUDE.md generation-run guidance.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/testutils/... -count=1 passes\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Tests cover matching outputs, divergent outputs, normalizers, and BuildBinary\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Tests skip gracefully when cmd/ source is absent (generation-run state)\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"pkg/format: implement HumanSize, color, and column alignment (srd003-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  descripti